course: dictionary
lesson: 8819
title: Shellfish and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A good word-detective looks at the words around a new word. «A gull drops a shellfish onto rocks from a height to smash the shell open.» The shell and the smashing tell you the animal has a hard covering, so a shellfish has a shell.
explain: Shellfish are water animals with a shell. Crabs, lobsters, prawns, mussels, oysters and clams are all shellfish. Look for them in the lists of sentences you read, such as «Rays hide in sand and eat shellfish and worms.»
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Otters find crabs and shellfish by feeling under stones.» If shellfish means water animals with a shell, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Shellfish are water animals with a shell, such as crabs, lobsters, prawns, mussels, oysters and clams.
fact: Many people eat shellfish, but it must be fresh and cooked properly to be safe.
fact: Shellfish are not always true fish: crabs, lobsters and shrimps are crustaceans, while mussels, oysters and scallops are molluscs.
fact: Some people have a shellfish allergy, which can be very dangerous, so food labels warn about shellfish.
fact: The word «shellfish» is usually the same for one animal and for many animals.
exercise: «A gull drops a shellfish onto rocks from a height to smash the shell open.» What is a shellfish? | A stone with a shell pattern | A fish with scales and fins | *A water animal with a shell, such as a crab or mussel | A bird that lives near rocks
exercise: «Asian small-clawed otters find crabs and shellfish by feeling under stones.» Which of these is a shellfish? | A pigeon | *A prawn | A trout | A frog
exercise: Food labels warn about shellfish. Why? | Shellfish are always sweet and sticky | *Some people are allergic to it, and that can be very dangerous | Shellfish can fly and must be kept in boxes | Shellfish are only sold in winter
test: Shellfish are not always true fish. Which of these is a crustacean, a kind of shellfish? | Salmon | Trout | *Lobster | Tuna
test: «Rays hide in sand and eat shellfish and worms.» What do rays eat, according to this sentence? | Bread and cheese | *Shellfish and worms | Grass and leaves | Apples and nuts
exam: «People allergic to shellfish may react to insects.» What does this sentence tell you? | Shellfish are safe for everyone to eat | *Some people's bodies react badly to shellfish, and the same people may react to insects | Insects are a type of shellfish | Insects only live in the sea
